{"task": "b2_perms10", "expected": 101042, "seed": 22, "arm": "B_medium_free", "effort": "medium", "budget": 1000000, "elapsed_s": 322.71, "error": null, "correct": true, "got": 101042, "finish_reason": "stop", "hit_max_tokens": false, "guillotine": false, "prompt_tokens": 78, "completion_tokens": 2398, "reasoning_chars": 6138, "answer_chars": 805, "tok_per_s": 7.62, "answer_tail": "\\dots, 9$ must alternate: either $+ - + - + - + - +$ or $- + - + - + - + -$.\n\nThese are precisely the alternating (zigzag) permutations of length 10. The number of alternating permutations of length $n$ starting with an up (pattern $< > < > \\cdots$) is the Euler zigzag number $E_n = A000111(n)$. By the complement symmetry $p_i \\mapsto 11 - p_i$, the number starting with a down is the same.\n\nFor $n = 10$, $E_{10} = 50521$. Therefore the total count is:\n\n$$2 \\times 50521 = 101042$$\n\nANSWER: 101042"}
{"task": "b2_perms10", "expected": 101042, "seed": 22, "arm": "D_medium_cut", "effort": "medium", "budget": 8192, "elapsed_s": 222.97, "error": null, "correct": false, "got": 50521, "finish_reason": "stop", "hit_max_tokens": false, "guillotine": false, "prompt_tokens": 78, "completion_tokens": 1492, "reasoning_chars": 3453, "answer_chars": 1004, "tok_per_s": 6.94, "answer_tail": "g (zigzag) permutation**: the comparisons between consecutive elements must alternate direction:\n- p\u2081 < p\u2082 > p\u2083 < p\u2084 > p\u2085 < ... or\n- p\u2081 > p\u2082 < p\u2083 > p\u2084 < p\u2085 > ...\n\n**Counting:** The number of alternating permutations of {1, 2, ..., n} is given by the **Euler zigzag numbers** (OEIS A000111):\n\n| n | Count |\n|---|-------|\n| 1 | 1 |\n| 2 | 1 |\n| 3 | 2 |\n| 4 | 5 |\n| 5 | 16 |\n| 6 | 61 |\n| 7 | 272 |\n| 8 | 1385 |\n| 9 | 7936 |\n| 10 | 50521 |\n\nFor n = 10, the Euler zigzag number is **50521**.\n\nANSWER: 50521"}
